---
import { FAQ } from '../data/faq';
import WhyEditableFrames from '../components/WhyEditableFrames.astro';
import AgentGuide from '../components/AgentGuide.astro';
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';import Playground from '../components/Playground';import studies from '../data/studies.json';
const description='Explore 12 editable code-generated video scenes. Play with 3D worlds, motion graphics and illustrated explainers, change the details, and save your own frame.';
---
<Page title="EditableFrames — Code-Generated Video You Can Edit" description={description} schema={[{'@type':'FAQPage',mainEntity:FAQ.map(({q,a})=>({'@type':'Question',name:q,acceptedAnswer:{'@type':'Answer',text:a}}))}]}>
<section class="hero"><div class="hero-kicker"><span class="live-dot"/> AN OPEN CANVAS FOR CODE-GENERATED VIDEO</div><div class="hero-line"><h1>What if every frame<br/>was <em>yours to change?</em></h1><div class="hero-stamp" aria-hidden="true"><span>GO ON,<br/>TOUCH IT.</span><b>↙</b></div></div><div class="hero-bottom"><p>EditableFrames is an open-source framework for code-generated video.<br/>Give each scene its own controls, then refine it with reversible edits.</p><a class="button primary" href="#playground">Find your frame <span>↓</span></a></div></section>
<div class="studio-wrap"><Playground client:visible/></div>
<section class="possibilities"><span class="mono">NOT A FIXED VISUAL LANGUAGE</span><p>A castle. A story. A signal.<br/><em>Same freedom to change your mind.</em></p><div class="capability-strip"><span>✳ Per-scene controls</span><span>↶ Reversible edits</span><span>◉ Canvas + Three.js studies</span><span>↗ Open to new libraries</span></div></section>
<section class="collection section" id="gallery"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">THE COLLECTION / 01—12</span><h2>Pick a world.<br/>Leave your fingerprints.</h2></div><p>Twelve editable studies. Five creative directions.<br/>Every one is a starting point, not a finished answer.</p></div><div class="genre-labels"><span>Product demos</span><span>3D worlds</span><span>Motion design</span><span>Explainers</span><span>Illustration</span></div><div class="gallery-grid">{studies.map((s,i)=><a class="study-card" href={`/genres/${s.scene}/`}><div class="card-image"><img src={`/demos/${s.scene}.jpg`} alt={s.detail} width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><span class="card-open" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><div class="card-meta"><span class="mono">{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')} / {s.genre}</span><span class="mono">{s.duration}s</span></div><h3>{s.title}</h3><p>{s.hook}</p></a>)}</div></section>
<AgentGuide/>
<section class="manifesto section"><span class="eyebrow">THE IDEA BEHIND EDITABLEFRAMES</span><div class="manifesto-grid"><h2>Make the code ambitious.<br/><em>Keep the details editable.</em></h2><div><p>EditableFrames is an open-source framework for videos created with code and refined by people or AI agents. A clip can expose its own colors, shapes, camera, timing and media as controls, with reversible changes.</p><p>The controls are an interface to a scene, not a limit on what it can become. New renderers and libraries can join as the ideas get more interesting.</p><a class="text-link" href="/guide/">Meet the framework ↗</a></div></div><div class="principles"><article><span>01 / CREATE</span><h3>Start with an idea.</h3><p>Write a scene yourself or work with a tool-capable agent. Keep your choice of creative library.</p></article><article><span>02 / REFINE</span><h3>Expose the right details.</h3><p>One clip needs a headline. Another needs a camera. Give each one its own set of useful controls.</p></article><article><span>03 / KEEP GOING</span><h3>Change your mind.</h3><p>Refine a detail, undo it, try again. Here, save a still or edit settings; use the local SDK for supported video exports.</p></article></div></section>
<WhyEditableFrames/>
<section class="faq section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">Q&A / A FEW GOOD QUESTIONS</span><h2 id="faq-heading">Curious is a<br/>good place to start.</h2></div><div>{FAQ.map(({q,a})=><details><summary>{q}</summary><p>{a}</p></details>)}</div></section>
<section class="closing section"><span class="eyebrow">YOUR NEXT FRAME IS WAITING</span><h2>A little less watching.<br/><em>A little more making.</em></h2><a href="#playground" class="button primary">Go make something yours ↑</a><a href="https://stitchable.ai/" class="text-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Use it in Stitchable Pro ↗</a></section>
</Page>
